# VS Code Local History - an embedded git repo, never ours to track
.history/

# Claude Code - per-turn and per-session state is regenerated every turn/session;
# settings.json and turn-config.json ARE tracked (see
# claude-hub/playbooks/onboard_a_project.md §5 - each of these markers needs its
# line added by hand in every consumer repo)
.claude/turn-state.json
**/.claude/turn-state.json
.claude/session-banner.json
**/.claude/session-banner.json
.claude/session-wrapup.json
**/.claude/session-wrapup.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# kicad-cli writes <name>-erc.rpt / <name>-drc.rpt into the working directory when
# --output is omitted. Generated on demand - regenerate, do not track.
*-erc.rpt
*-drc.rpt

# The printable documents - DERIVED from the prose by tools/md2html.py and
# tools/make-pdf.ps1, plus the print-sized photo copies they scale on the way. Regenerate,
# do not track: a tracked copy would be a second source of truth that silently goes stale,
# which is the exact failure STATUS.md and INDEX.md are generated to avoid.
#
#   build-document  <- machine/assembly.md    how to build it. ~18 pages, no photographs
#   design-record   <- the twelve chapters    why it is that shape. ~102 pages, all
#                                             sixteen photographs embedded
#   wiring-document <- the five wiring/*.md   power in, the E-stops, the drives, the ground
#                                             bar. Added 2026-11-07 because a .md file is
#                                             unreadable outside an editor
#   shop-pack       <- docs/drawings/        what to make. The fourteen plate sheets for
#                      shop-pack.html        the machining visit - and the one that gets
#                                            emailed out. Its HTML IS tracked and is
#                                            hand-authored, so only the PDF is derived.
#
# Every reader document lives in docs/ since 2026-11-11 - his call, one folder for all of
# them. docs/panel-schematic.html is NOT here: it is hand-authored and tracked, like
# shop-pack.
docs/build-document.html
docs/build-document.pdf
docs/design-record.html
docs/design-record.pdf
docs/wiring-document.html
docs/wiring-document.pdf
docs/drawings/board-mounting.pdf
docs/drawings/shop-pack.pdf
build-photos/

# The send-out bundle - four derived or already-tracked files in one attachment, built by
# tools/make-bundle.ps1 at the end of a pack print. Every member is in the repo or
# generated from it, so the zip is a convenience and never a source.
docs/drawings/CNC Build.zip

# tools/ gets imported as modules by the pack checks
__pycache__/
